common='Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space and μ any measure. Let D be a bounded positive real-linear operator on L²(μ;ℝ); positivity includes selfadjointness. There exists a bounded positive REAL operator Γ with Γ²=D, and for EVERY real L² class u, ‖Γu‖²=⟨Du,u⟩ℝ. No CFC instance, complex extension, root, finite/probability measure or finite-dimensional L² is a hypothesis.'
